.TH WAVE-DOCTOR 1 "" "LinuxWave" "LinuxWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-doctor \- Look for things that are already broken but rarely noticed: a version directory without its executable, a dangling link, a package that was never linked, an orphaned dependency tree, an ELF file whose RPATH still names an absolute path. Nothing is changed; every finding comes with the command that fixes it. The exit status is the number of problems found.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave doctor [check ...] [\-\-raw] [\-\-list\-checks]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Look for things that are already broken but rarely noticed: a version
directory without its executable, a dangling link, a package that was
never linked, an orphaned dependency tree, an ELF file whose RPATH still
names an absolute path. Nothing is changed; every finding comes with the
command that fixes it. The exit status is the number of problems found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Machine-readable: one 'severity<TAB>check<TAB>detail' line per finding
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
List the check names and what each one looks at

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave doctor
wave doctor links
wave doctor --raw
wave doctor --list-checks
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
